    "facts": "On demand, he failed to produce licence for sale of food articles.\nThe sample of the food was also taken for analysis from the shop.\nThe accused examined two witnesses in defence.\nThe accused was convicted and sentenced by the learned Magistrate after completion of the trial on of 27.7.2005.\nThe shop was rented out to Vineet Kumar.\nIt was prepared on .\n30.9.2004.\nThe licence would be deemed to be valid on and after 30.9.2004.\nHe got the licence renewed only on of 30.9.2004.\n6.\nHe has obtained the licence w.e.f. 30.9.2004.\nThe Food Inspector had visited the shop in the absence of Vineet Kumar.\nThus, the learned Sessions Judge, Shimla, has correctly come to the conclusion that it was not the accused who was running the shop/Dhaba without possessing the licence under the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act and Rules.\n",
